        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hermann Giesler, Albert Speer, Adolf Hitler\n- Roles: architect, Reich Minister of Armaments and War Production\n- Organizations: Nazi Germany\n- Topics: Nazi era, World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Hermann Giesler was born on April 2, 1898, in Siegen.\n- Albert Speer was born on March 19, 1905.\n- Hermann Giesler was a German architect during the Nazi era.\n- Adolf Hitler most favored and rewarded Hermann Giesler and Albert Speer among architects.\n- Albert Speer was a German architect.\n- For most of World War II, Albert Speer served as Reich Minister of Armaments and War Production for Nazi Germany.\n- Albert Speer died on September 1, 1981.\n- Hermann Giesler died on January 20, 1987, in Düsseldorf.",
